> Best idea yet! let's go with it. But what does .ui do  in a sentence?


It means that your happiness is associated with that word.

According to the proposed usage:

.ui do klama
My happiness is associated with you coming (I'm not saying whether or not
you can and do come, though.)

do .ui klama
You come, and I am happy that YOU came.


I support the proposal. I find it more elegant than the current system,
which requires the difficult memorization of an arbitrary distinction.





